The four fonts here are bundled into sci_anim unchanged, and Typst sees no others.

- LibertinusSans-Regular.otf is from the Libertinus 7.051 release,
  https://github.com/alerque/libertinus/releases/download/v7.051/Libertinus-7.051.zip
  (sha256 4d9be29b5cb380c35af8ba967abcc752ad1e07be1f738a9789c33e0dd7478c92), static/OTF/.
- LibertinusSerif-Regular.otf is from the typst-assets 0.15.1 crate
  (https://github.com/typst/typst-assets), files/fonts/. It is byte for byte the file of the
  same name in the Libertinus 7.051 release.
- NewCMMath-Regular.otf is from the typst-assets 0.15.1 crate, files/fonts/.
- JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf is from the JetBrains Mono 2.304 release,
  https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono/releases/download/v2.304/JetBrainsMono-2.304.zip
  (sha256 6f6376c6ed2960ea8a963cd7387ec9d76e3f629125bc33d1fdcd7eb7012f7bbf), fonts/ttf/.
  Libertinus Mono is not used: it lacks │ (U+2502), which tree and box-drawn tables print, and
  ✓, ✗ and ❯, which terminal tools print.

Libertinus Sans and Libertinus Serif are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, in
LICENSE-OFL.txt, which is the release's OFL.txt. JetBrains Mono is licensed under the SIL Open
Font License 1.1, in LICENSE-OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt, which is the release's OFL.txt.

New Computer Modern Math is licensed under the GUST Font License 1.0, in LICENSE-GUST.txt,
which is the GUST section of typst-assets' NOTICE. NewCM10-Regular, the one New Computer Modern
file under GPL-3.0 with a font exception, is not bundled.
